// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// rules/pre/ - before a single sheet is opened. Copy this file, rename it, delete this header.
//
//   Name it  <Topic>Rules.cs  and name the class the same: InputsRules.cs holds InputsRules.
//
//   Rename to `.cs`. A `.template` file is not scanned, which is the only reason this one can sit
//   here without the run trying to execute it.
//
// When it runs   First, before anything is read. A rule failing here costs nothing, because
//                nothing has been opened yet - which is the point of the folder: file names,
//                settings and the environment are checkable without the data.
//
// What you get   IPreContext, and it is the smallest of the four:
//
//                context.Option(...)   settings from the recipe's Validation.Options
//                context.Files(...)    a folder scanned, to check what is and is not there
//                context.Json(...)     a JSON file read
//                context.Error/Warn/Info(message)
//
// Not here       No `Tables` and no `context.Schema` - the sheets have not been read, so the
//                accessor does not exist yet. The type says so: those names are not on
//                IPreContext, so reaching for one is a red squiggle rather than a run that gets
//                this far and stops. **This file has one using line, not two**: a
//                `using Tabbit.Rules;` here is a compile error.
//
//                Reporting cannot point at a cell either, for the same reason. Messages here are
//                about the run rather than about a row.
//
// Priority       [RulePriority(-10)] on the class puts it in an earlier tier - see rules/global/.
//
// This folder is flat. A file one level down is not run at all; put shared helpers in
// rules/shared/.
//
// Full guide: doc/validation.md
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

